# Pace — Project Context

> **Source of truth.** Every future session reads this BEFORE changing anything, inspects the existing code, and updates this file when a product/architecture decision changes. Keep the DECISION here, not the story behind it. (`docs/` and `README.md` predate multi-user and may be stale — this file wins.)

---

## 1. Product

Pace answers one question: **"How much can I spend today and still stay on track for my savings target?"**

It is a **dynamic spending trajectory, not a fixed daily budget**. It shows the *consequence* of today's spending on every future day; it never tells the user what they *should* spend. Pace is currently a **working production MVP in real-world validation** (owner + one friend + guest demo).

**Philosophy (locked):**
- Reduce finance to **one understandable daily signal**; useful *at the moment of spending*, not for review.
- Show consequences, don't prescribe; the user stays in control.
- Savings target is protected by the trajectory. Underspending raises future pace; overspending lowers it.
- Do NOT turn Pace into a budgeting/accounting dashboard (no charts, categories, dashboard expansion).
- **Do not add features because they are possible. Prefer observing real usage before expanding.**

---

> **Money Model V2 (Steps 1–3) is LIVE in production since 2026-09-20 (Apps Script v12 + Netlify `6ab00a1dd3d6617cbc465293`) and supersedes the legacy formula below for the Pace-defining fields.** Profiles without an established `current_balance` get NO Pace (`needs_position`) until they complete the position setup screen — this is intentional, not a bug. See the "Money Model V2" bullets in §3.

## 2. Pace algorithm (exact — DO NOT change without an explicit product decision)

Settings (per profile): `monthly_income`, `monthly_savings_target`, `fixed_monthly_expenses`, `starting_balance`, `starting_balance_date` (+ legacy display-only `metro_weekday_cost`, `weekly_auto_cost`, not in the math).

```
discretionary_monthly = income - savings_target - fixed_expenses
period                = later of (starting_balance_date, 1st of month) .. month end
total_spendable       = discretionary_monthly * period_days / days_in_month
today_pace            = max(total_spendable - expenses_before_today, 0) / days_remaining_incl_today
remaining_spendable   = total_spendable - expenses_through_today          (may be negative)
remaining_pace        = max(remaining_spendable, 0) / days_remaining_after_today   (0 on last day)
```
- **Invariant:** `today_pace(day N) == remaining_pace(day N-1)`. Paces never negative; no NaN/Infinity; values rounded to 2dp for output, compared at full precision.
- **Today's own spend never changes today's `today_pace`**; it changes the future (`remaining_pace`). Overspend is counted once.
- `status` = `spent_today` vs `today_pace` with `eps = max(0.5, today_pace*0.005)`: `over` / `under` / `on_track`; `over` also if `remaining_spendable <= 0`.
- `current_balance = starting_balance + income_since_start − expenses_since_start`.
- Savings invariant: `income − fixed − cumulative_flexible_expenses >= savings_target` while spending stays within the pool.
- **State fields:** `as_of, inputs, month{key,day_of_month,days_in_month,days_in_period,days_elapsed,days_remaining,days_remaining_incl_today}, discretionary_monthly, total_spendable, initial_daily_pace, today_pace, spent_today, expected_today, today_variance, remaining_spendable, remaining_pace, expected_spend_to_date, actual_spend_to_date, income_this_month, pace, status, current_balance, transaction_count` (+ back-compat aliases `daily_allowance`=today_pace, `remaining_discretionary`=remaining_spendable, `safe_daily_for_rest_of_month`=remaining_pace). Backend is authoritative; the frontend **never recomputes finances** except a best-effort optimistic mirror (§5).
- **"Today" = the user's device-local calendar day** (`localDayKey()`, never `toISOString`). The client sends `today` (YYYY-MM-DD) with every request; the backend derives today/month boundaries from it with integer calendar math (falls back to server date `Asia/Kolkata` only if absent). No timezone UI.

---

## 3. Architecture

**Stack (intentionally simple; do not add a DB/framework prematurely):** plain HTML/CSS/vanilla JS (no build, no dependencies, no web fonts) → Netlify (`https://pace-ledger.netlify.app`); Google Apps Script web app (JSON over `doGet`/`doPost`); Google Sheet as storage.

**Repo:** `frontend/{index.html,styles.css,app.js,config.js}` (deploy = these 4 files zipped; `config.js` holds the public `/exec` URL) · `apps-script/Code.gs` (+ `Code.gs.v8.bak` = pre-multi-user rollback, `appsscript.json`) · `tests/` · `backups/` · `docs/` (stale).

**Production IDs:** spreadsheet `1rG4C9S0_5mVGSLrvGWv8_5sQLrHD8orWMtX0bcJQYmc`; bound Apps Script `16F5bqIdgh7hLN4GLNJ148GINDPLNqGgOMihP7KP9-ljm60CK4T-C9Ybp`; web app deployment "Untitled" (URL in `config.js`, execute as owner, access Anyone).

### Multi-user (LIVE since 2026-09-20)
- **Profiles:** `MUHAMMED` (private), `FRIEND` (private), `GUEST` (shared demo, no code). One spreadsheet, per-profile tabs: `USERS` (`user_key | access_credential_hash | tx_sheet | settings_sheet | mode | active`), `TX_MUH`/`SET_MUH`, `TX_FRIEND`/`SET_FRIEND`, `TX_GUEST`/`SET_GUEST`. Legacy `Transactions`/`Settings` tabs are **untouched backups, no longer read**.
- **Transaction row:** `Date | Amount | Note | Type | ID` (ID = stable UUID `transaction_id`, never derived from index/date/amount, survives edit). Types: expense/income (UI logs expenses).
- **Auth (lightweight private-MVP access — NOT OAuth; Google Auth was deliberately abandoned as unnecessary complexity):** `POST login {profile, code}` compares `SHA-256(code)` to the hash in `USERS` → returns a **stateless HMAC-SHA256-signed session token** (`SESSION_SECRET` in Script Properties; 30-day expiry private, 24h guest). `POST guest {}` issues a GUEST token. Every other action needs `token`; `resolveCtx_` verifies signature+expiry → `USERS` row (active) → that profile's tabs. **Client-supplied `user_key`/sheet names are never used for authorization.** Defenses: tab names must match `^TX_`/`^SET_`; per-user idempotency namespace; 8 failed logins/profile → 15-min lock; `active=false` revokes (≤5 min cache lag); deleting `SESSION_SECRET` logs everyone out. Only hashes are stored — **access codes live only with the owner, never in source/sheet/frontend/this file.** To rotate a code, replace its hash in `USERS!B2` (Muhammed) / `B3` (Friend).
- **Money Model V2 — Step 1 (backend data model only; LIVE 2026-09-20, Apps Script v12):** per-profile Settings gain optional keys `display_name` (human label, ≤40 chars, never an identity/credential), `currency` (INR/MAD/IQD/RUB display unit, no FX), `current_balance` (≥0; money the user really has NOW; user-established, never derived, never auto-changed at month boundaries), `current_balance_date` (YYYY-MM-DD **local** day it was established; stored as text; defaults to the client's local day on save; never rewritten by reads), `minimum_daily_spend` (≥0, optional, 0/absent = none; a future realism constraint — NOT a commitment, not an expense, not deducted, not a savings change). Written only through the existing `saveMoneyPlan` (all V2 fields optional ⇒ legacy payloads still work and never clobber stored V2 values). **Legacy `starting_balance`/`starting_balance_date` are kept unchanged and are NOT the V2 balance** (`starting_balance_date` is the Pace period start; `starting_balance` feeds derived `state.current_balance`); no balance is ever invented for existing users. `metro_weekday_cost`/`weekly_auto_cost` are DEPRECATED legacy rows (still physically present, never read by any logic, not part of the plan model). `plan` gains `setup_state` = `needs_plan` | `needs_position` (valid plan, no balance yet — Muhammed/Friend today) | `complete` (Guest demo always) plus the V2 fields; `needs_setup` remains only as an alias of `setup_state==='needs_plan'`. **`calculateState` is unchanged in Step 1** (V2 Pace formula, onboarding UI, minimum-vs-pace logic come in later steps).
- **Money Model V2 — Step 1.5 (commitment foundation; LIVE 2026-09-20, Apps Script v12):** a commitment is `{id, name, amount, status, paid_at}` (JSON in the `commitments` setting). `id` = stable, immutable, backend-generated (`cm_…`), never an index/name/amount, never reused (deleted ids and forged/unknown ids are rejected). `status` = `unpaid`|`paid`; `paid_at` = client-LOCAL `YYYY-MM-DD` (defaults to the client's day when marking paid; cleared when unpaid; contradictions rejected). **Legacy `{name,amount}` commitments default to `unpaid`, never inferred paid**; their id is derived deterministically per profile on read (stable across reads, nothing written) and becomes the persisted id on the next legitimate save; old id-less client payloads are matched to existing commitments by exact name so ids/paid state survive. Mutated only through the existing `saveMoneyPlan` (no new endpoint). `plan.remaining_commitments = SUM(unpaid)` is the contract **Step 2 will consume** (paid commitments stop being protected); `fixed_monthly_expenses` stays the total of ALL commitments so `calculateState` is unchanged in Step 1.5. No transaction matching/UPI/bank logic exists: future transaction sources plug in through a separate activity/matching layer that flips `status`; commitment storage never reads transactions.
- **Money Model V2 — Step 2 (position-based Pace engine; LIVE 2026-09-20, Apps Script v12):** pure `calculatePaceV2_(input)` (no Sheets/auth/mutation; deterministic) + `applyPaceV2_` mapping onto the state. `B`=`current_balance` is an ANCHOR (never mutated/derived/reset monthly/auto-increased by income); `E`=sum of `type==='expense'` transactions dated on/after `current_balance_date` and ≤ today (historical, future, income ignored; YYYY-MM-DD local-day compare only); `protected = savings_target + SUM(unpaid commitments)` (each counted once; paid ones are NOT protected; `fixed_monthly_expenses`, income, `starting_balance*`, metro/auto, `minimum_daily_spend` are NOT used); `remaining_flexible = B − E − protected`; `D` = whole local days left in the calendar month INCLUDING today (period ends at month end; balance carries across months). `today_pace = start-of-day flexible / D` (today's own spend never moves it), `tomorrow_pace = remaining_flexible / (D−1)` (null on the last day), so today_pace(N)==tomorrow_pace(N−1); under/overspending needs no carry variable. Negative flexible ⇒ `pace_status:'behind'` (shown pace 0, raw negative in `today_pace_unclamped`/`remaining_flexible`). `minimum_daily_spend>0`: `below_minimum` iff flexible≥0 and pace<minimum; gap = max(0,min−pace), gap_total = gap×D; the minimum NEVER changes the pace. `pace_status` ∈ on_pace | below_minimum | behind | needs_position. No established position (missing/corrupt/future `current_balance(_date)`) or no plan ⇒ no Pace (`state.position_ready=false`, `state.v2.reason`, legacy pace fields 0, `status:'on_track'`), never a fallback to starting_balance/income/old formula; the engine never repairs stored data. State keeps every legacy field (frontend-compatible): `today_pace/daily_allowance/remaining_pace/remaining_spendable/status/…` now come from V2 (`remaining_spendable`=remaining_flexible, `remaining_pace`=tomorrow_pace, `status` keeps over/under/on_track), full result in `state.v2`, plus `state.pace_status`/`state.position_ready`/`state.pace_engine:'v2'`. Legacy month-view/total fields and `state.current_balance` (from starting_balance) remain only for compatibility and are not the Pace model. Guest demo has an explicit position (`current_balance` 45000) that an old Guest tab self-heals.
- **Money Model V2 — Step 3 (onboarding + position setup; LIVE 2026-09-20, Apps Script v12):** ONE setup state machine = `plan.setup_state`. `needs_plan` (new/unconfigured private profile) → 6-step onboarding (name, currency, monthly income >0, savings ≥0, current balance ≥0, optional commitments; nothing else is asked — no minimum_daily_spend/metro/auto/period/salary date) saved in ONE atomic `saveMoneyPlan {require_complete:true,…}` (name, currency, income>0, balance all required; backend re-validates; `current_balance_date` = client local day; commitments sent id-less ⇒ backend ids, `unpaid`; a profile that is ALREADY set up rejects `require_complete` so a stale draft can never overwrite newer data). `needs_position` (existing valid plan, no balance: Muhammed/Friend today) → single question "How much money do you have available right now?" saved via `saveMoneyPlan {position_only:true, current_balance}`: writes ONLY `current_balance(+_date)` (+ `currency`/`display_name` only if still empty — a stored one is never overwritten); income/savings/commitments/transactions/`starting_balance*` are never touched, never used as a default. Existing local currency is preserved and persisted to the backend at setup. Balance below savings/commitments is accepted (state `behind`, not a validation error). Guest is never onboarded. Interrupted onboarding keeps a per-profile browser-local draft (`pace_draft_<USER>`, no secrets, cleared on success/logout) that the server always overrides. Onboarding is a planning input: no income transaction, no income added to the balance.
> **Step 2 must not be deployed by itself. Existing users without current_balance require the position setup flow before V2 Pace is exposed to them.** (Step 3 provides that flow; deploy Steps 1–3 together, backend first.) The old main screen still maps V2 states onto the legacy over/under/on_track look (a `behind` user reads "OVER PACE · 0") until the main-screen step.
- **Money Model V2 — Step 4 (main screen = pure presentation of `state.v2`; LIVE 2026-09-20, frontend only):** diagnostic on the real ₹12,130 case proved the ENGINE was right (B 12,130, E 448 all dated today, S 10,000, C 16,500 [a single legacy "Fixed expenses" line] ⇒ flexible −14,818, behind); the problem was the screen still mapping legacy fields (`status`, `remaining_spendable`, `remaining_pace`, old bar/left/over comparison, `state.current_balance` from `starting_balance`). Now the main screen reads ONLY `state.v2` (backend is the single source of truth; no formula in app.js — the one local mirror is the optimistic shift by the logged amount, replaced by the server response): `pace_status` ⇒ word ON PACE / BELOW MINIMUM / BEHIND / POSITION NEEDED (text carries the state, colour only reinforces); `today_pace` (start-of-day, never moved by today's spending) shown big; `expenses_today` = "spent today"; `tomorrow_pace` = "From tomorrow" (— on the last day); `remaining_flexible` = "Remaining flexible" (negative shown as a red deficit, never clamped away; BEHIND line "₹X short of protecting your plan"); `protected_money` = "Protected" (savings + UNPAID commitments); `days_remaining_incl_today` = "Days left · incl. today"; below_minimum shows `minimum_spend_gap`/`_total` as a secondary line and never changes the pace. `needs_position` is normally intercepted by the setup flow; if it ever reaches the main screen it shows POSITION NEEDED with — (never ₹0/day). Month/Balance sheets and Settings use V2 (`current_balance` = the declared anchor; effective balance = `v2.effective_balance`); legacy `state.status/remaining_spendable/remaining_pace/current_balance` and metro/auto rows are compatibility aliases only and are NOT authoritative. Greeting ("Good morning/afternoon/evening, <display_name>." from device time) is shown on the main screen only, hidden for Guest and when no name is set. No production data was touched in this step.
- **Money Model V2 — Step 5 (Money Plan editable Current Balance; LOCAL ONLY, NOT deployed):** Money Plan edit page = MONTHLY INCOME, SAVINGS TARGET, CURRENT BALANCE ("How much money you have available right now.", "As of <date>"), COMMITTED EXPENSES; review shows Monthly income / Savings target / Current balance / Committed expenses plus the backend dry-run Pace preview. Current balance is a declared ANCHOR, never a transaction: an explicit balance save sets `current_balance` = entered value and `current_balance_date` = the device's local calendar day (server default from the client `today`; no date picker, no backdating), so earlier transactions stop being deducted and expenses on/after that day count. Only fields the user actually CHANGES are sent: balance-only edit → existing `saveMoneyPlan` `position_only` (writes just the two position cells); plan edit → full save, `current_balance` included only if changed (income/savings/commitment edits never reset the anchor or its date); nothing changed → no request. Validation unchanged (≥0 numeric; below savings/commitments/income allowed → BEHIND). Failure ⇒ nothing written, entered values kept. Transactions, ids, commitments (legacy single "Fixed expenses" not split, nothing auto-paid), savings, income, `starting_balance` untouched by a balance edit. needs_position users still establish it via the Step 3 position screen (same endpoint); needs_plan still onboards; Guest unchanged. No backend change was needed (Code.gs == v12); frontend only + 21 tests (S5-1…21; suite 379 green). Field name stays `monthly_income`.
- **Money Model V2 — Step 5.5 (balance semantics correction + commitment paid/unpaid; LOCAL ONLY, NOT deployed):** `current_balance` = a SNAPSHOT of "the money I actually have available right now" at the moment it is declared (not income / starting / start-of-day / derived / a transaction; never creates or mutates a transaction). Because it already reflects everything spent so far, Pace must not deduct that spending again. Transactions have only Date/Amount/Note/Type/ID (NO timestamp), so same-day before/after cannot be told from the transaction; instead the save records the snapshot by id: settings row `current_balance_covered` = JSON array of the expense ids dated from the anchor day to today that existed at save time (additive; absent = legacy anchor = old rule, no migration; id-less legacy rows count as covered; `current_balance_date` stays the local calendar day, no `toISOString`, no server time). Engine (`calculatePaceV2_`): counted expenses = expense tx dated on/after the anchor date, ≤ today, NOT in `covered`; `effective = B − counted`; `flexible = effective − (savings + UNPAID commitments)`. **Anchor day** (`current_balance_date == today`): today is already accounted for → `today_pace = flexible / (days after today)` (`pace_days`; last day of month ⇒ /1), tomorrow_pace same, and it moves with spending logged AFTER the snapshot; **later days**: `today_pace = start-of-day flexible / days incl. today` (unchanged rule). `v2.expenses_today` = everything logged today (display), `expenses_counted_today`/`expenses_since_balance` = what is actually deducted; new fields `anchor_day`, `pace_days`. A new balance is a new snapshot: previous anchor + covered list replaced; expenses dated before the new anchor date never count (a backfilled expense dated earlier is ignored); missing/corrupt anchor ⇒ no Pace. Examples locked in tests: 12,588 (448 already logged) − 10,000, commitments paid ⇒ flexible 2,588 ⇒ ₹258.80/day over 10 days; then a ₹200 expense ⇒ 2,388 ⇒ ₹238.80; unpaid 16,500 ⇒ −13,912 BEHIND; 20,000 − 10,000 − 5,000 unpaid ⇒ 500/day, marked PAID ⇒ 1,000/day. Commitments: Money Plan edit page has a per-commitment PAID / NOT YET PAID toggle (44px); paid ⇒ `status:'paid'`, `paid_at` = client local day, NOT protected; unpaid ⇒ paid_at cleared, protected again; no transaction is created, nothing is inferred or auto-marked, the legacy single "Fixed expenses" line is not split (user decides). Savings target is never touched by these rules. Frontend: entered balance = Review value = server value (dry-run preview uses the same payload); writes bump a data epoch and a background load that started before a write is discarded (stale cache/read can't overwrite a newer balance). Limitation: the snapshot is by transaction id, so editing a covered same-day expense's date later or logging a same-day expense with a stale device clock isn't distinguished; a proper per-transaction timestamp would need a new column (not added). Displayed amounts round to whole units (258.80 shows ₹259).
- **Today screen — FINAL UI decision (supersedes the rejected full-screen "ledger" redesign; frontend only, LOCAL, NOT deployed):** Today is a Pace-first daily view. The Pace slider/trajectory is a core visual feature showing the user's spending position. The user's expense list functions as the integrated ledger within the page. The notebook aesthetic supports both. Order: masthead/nav (Today active) → dateline + small italic greeting (device local time; none for Guest / no display name) → status word (ON PACE / BELOW MINIMUM / BEHIND; never OVER/UNDER) + its line → TODAY'S PACE (`v2.today_pace`, one of the largest numbers) → **Pace slider** (thin outlined track with ticks, notch = "today's line", `aria-hidden`, presentation only; fill = `expenses_counted_today ÷ today_pace` scaled to the line and never past it unless the server says BEHIND, when it runs past the line; BELOW MINIMUM = hatched fill showing today_pace as a share of `minimum_daily_spend`; no new finance) → "₹X spent today" (`expenses_today`) and "₹Y left" / "₹Y short" (`|remaining_flexible|`, red when short; no "over/remaining spendable") → From tomorrow (`tomorrow_pace`) → compact Remaining flexible / Protected / Days left rows → Today's expenses (newest first, ruled lines, "See all →" sheet) → "+ Log an expense". Do not redesign this into a dashboard or a full ledger.
- **Guest:** shared `TX_GUEST` demo (income 45,000 / savings 10,000 / fixed 16,500, ~10 entries), 300-row cap, `resetGuest` (guest session only) wipes+reseeds. Friend defaults (income 30,000 / savings 5,000 / fixed 10,000 / balance 0) are seeded in `SET_FRIEND`.
- **Money Plan (LIVE in production since 2026-09-20):** each profile edits its own income / savings target / commitments in the app (first-run setup + Settings → Edit Money Plan). Stored in the existing per-profile Settings tab: `monthly_income`, `monthly_savings_target`, `fixed_monthly_expenses` (= SUM of commitments, computed by the backend) and `commitments` (JSON `[{name,amount}]`). API `saveMoneyPlan {plan:{income,savings,commitments[],dry_run?}}` (POST, token) validates (numbers ≥ 0, savings+commitments ≤ income, ≤30 items, names ≤40) and returns `{settings, plan, state}`; `dry_run` = authoritative preview, writes nothing. `all`/`resetGuest` also return `plan {needs_setup, editable, income, savings, fixed, commitments, available}`. Setup shows only when `needs_setup` (income missing/invalid, or a present value invalid) — valid existing settings are never prompted/overwritten; a legacy fixed total with no breakdown shows as one “Fixed expenses” line. `starting_balance(_date)` are defaulted only when missing (first setup) and never overwritten. Guest: fixed demo plan, `saveMoneyPlan` refused. **Periods stay calendar months; a custom period-start/salary-cycle day is NOT supported** (needs an algorithm change — see §8).
- **Frontend session/cache:** **persistent per-profile sessions**: `{token,user,mode}` in `localStorage` `pace_session_<USER>` + `pace_active_profile` pointer (access code/hash never stored; legacy `pace_session_v1` migrated). Boot: active valid session → Pace paints from cache instantly, one background `all` reconciles; no login screen. Token `e` checked locally (expired → slot+cache cleared, gate shows "Session expired. Please sign in again."). Cache and currency are **per profile** (`pace_cache_v1_<USER>`, `pace_currency_<USER>`). **Switch user** only clears the active pointer (keeps sessions+caches; a profile with a saved session reopens with no code); **Log out** (Settings) removes only the current profile's session+cache. Server `unauthorized` or `user.key` mismatch clears that profile's session+cache → gate. Network failure ≠ invalid session (keep session+cache, show sync note). Tradeoff: saved-session profiles open without a code on that device until expiry/logout. **Entry screen (LIVE since 2026-09-20, Apps Script v11):** profile-agnostic Welcome (PACE / “Know your money. Stay on pace.” / SIGN IN / EXPLORE AS GUEST / ⓘ About sheet) → Sign in asks only for the access code; `login {code}` (no `profile`) lets the backend find the single active private user whose SHA-256 matches (ambiguous or no match = failed attempt; lockout counter `fail_ANY`, 8/15 min); legacy `login {profile, code}` still works. No hardcoded profile choices in the UI; Switch user/Log out/expired session return to Welcome (expired shows “Session expired. Please sign in again.”). A signed-in session bypasses Welcome. Motion (CSS only, reduced-motion respected): one-time-per-session ~600ms staggered reveal, ~200ms Welcome↔Sign-in section swap, About = ruled paper note sheet with focus trap + Escape + focus return. Notebook grid is ONE set of CSS vars (`--lh 34px, --grid-y, --row-shift, --margin-x, --page-pad-l, --ledger-rule`): headings and the code input end ON a rule, text rows start at rule+`--row-shift` (baseline on the line), About note uses the same vars. Welcome shows a hand-drawn SVG ink path with a small red "today" dot in the MIDDLE of it (past on the left, future on the right; deliberately no arrow, no upward trend), decorative, stroke-draw intro, built not yet deployed. Wordmark typography is shared vars (`--brand-font/style/weight/tracking`: serif italic 700, -0.01em) used by the masthead and the Welcome PACE.

### API contract (all POST, body JSON sent as `text/plain` to avoid CORS preflight)
- Public: `login`, `guest`. Session (`token` required, plus `today`): `all` → `{user, settings, transactions, state}`; `addTransaction` (`client_id` idempotent 90s, `date`) → `{transaction, state}`; `updateTransaction{transaction_id, amount?, note?}` → `{transaction, state}`; `deleteTransaction{transaction_id}` (idempotent; already-absent = success) → `{deleted_transaction_id, already_absent, state}`; `resetGuest`. `GET` = unauthenticated `?action=ping` only (no data over GET; token never in a URL).
- All writes serialized with `LockService`; correction ops re-locate the row by `transaction_id` under the lock; backend recalculates and returns authoritative state.

---

## 4. Frontend behavior (settled decisions)

- **Instant startup:** valid per-profile cached state paints immediately (no skeleton), then one background `all` replaces it; on failure keep cache + subtle "Sync unavailable" note. Guest shows the shell instantly and gets its session in the background.
- **Optimistic Add/Undo/Edit/Delete:** UI updates immediately from one optimistic state (`computeOptimistic`: applies the incremental effect of one amount to the already-computed aggregates; `today_pace` untouched); the backend response reconciles authoritatively; failures perform **surgical rollback** (exact row/values restored, that op's delta reversed). Cache is written only from confirmed server state. `client_id` idempotency for Add; `transaction_id` identifies persisted rows; `opInFlight[id]` blocks conflicting ops on one row; temp rows have Edit/Delete disabled until confirmed.
- **Undo:** bar "₹X logged — Undo" appears in the same tick as the optimistic row, 8s window (`UNDO_WINDOW_MS`), targets only the most recent transaction; Undo before server confirm cancels locally then deletes the server-written row by real id.
- **Reliability:** every request has a 15s `AbortController` timeout; **one retry** only for GET, or POST with a `client_id`, and only for transient failures (never for server business errors).
- **Large-expense warning:** sanity check, never a limit — amount > 5× `today_pace` OR > 25% of positive `remaining_spendable` (constants `LARGE_EXPENSE_PACE_MULTIPLIER`/`LARGE_EXPENSE_REMAINING_RATIO`) shows an in-sheet Cancel/Log confirmation; recomputed each submit; Enter can't bypass.
- **Multi-currency V1:** INR ₹, MAD د.م., IQD ع.د, RUB ₽ — **display unit only, no conversion, no FX** (₹45,000 just becomes د.م. 45,000). Central `formatMoney`/`money()` via `Intl.NumberFormat` (INR Indian grouping; MAD comma grouping; RUB space grouping/symbol after; Latin digits). Currency choice is per-device/per-profile in `localStorage`, not in the Sheet.
- **Edit** = amount + note only (same id); Edit/Delete act on the Today's-entries sheet; secondary areas via bottom sheets: Month, Balance, Today, Settings (profile, currency, Money Plan + Edit, Switch user, Log out, Reset demo for guest). Money Plan setup/edit is a full ledger page (steps: income → savings → commitments → review with backend-computed pace preview → “Start my Pace”); save applies the previewed state optimistically, then reconciles; failure restores the previous state and reopens the review with an error.

**UI/UX (intentionally locked — do not redesign without explicit instruction):** warm paper/account-book/ledger aesthetic; one continuous notebook page with horizontal ruling + red margin line; serif headings/status; monospace/tabular money; restrained red for over-pace (stronger only when severely over; extreme overspend shows "You spent a lot today." stamp); mobile-first (375–430 verified), centered "page" on desktop; **Today-focused**. Main-screen order: status (UNDER/ON/OVER PACE) → diff sentence → today's pace + bar → from-tomorrow pace / remaining spendable / days remaining → today's expenses → Log an expense. NO dark/fintech look, glassmorphism, generic SaaS cards, speedometer/dial, unnecessary charts/categories. Accessibility: 44px targets, focus-visible, aria labels (Settings gear labelled), Escape closes sheets, reduced-motion respected.

---

## 5. Performance decisions

Apps Script latency dominates: `all` ≈ 3–6s, POST ≈ 3–5s (one 136s stall seen); backend reads settings + all of the profile's transactions and recomputes every call, so payload/read cost grows with history. Frontend render is negligible (shell <100ms). Hence: cache-first startup, optimistic mutations, one request per action with no follow-up GET, timeout+single retry, no polling/timers. Do not "fix" latency by changing the backend model without an explicit decision.

---

## 6. Current production state (2026-09-20)

- **Live and verified (2026-09-20):** Apps Script **Version 12** (Money Model V2 Steps 1–3, same `/exec` URL) + Netlify deploy `6ab012dc762d7bd31cd715fe` (Step 4 main-screen V2 presentation on top of Step 3 onboarding + Welcome; backend NOT redeployed for Step 4 — still v12). Post-deploy smoke: backend 20/20 (auth, needs_position safety, POST-only, no secrets), Guest UI (Add/Undo/Reset, demo Pace) OK, Muhammed (103 tx) + Friend (1 tx) transactions/ids/settings byte-identical to the pre-deploy baseline. **Current production behavior:** Muhammed and Friend are `needs_position` (valid plan, no `current_balance`): the backend returns NO Pace for them and the app shows the position screen ("How much money do you have available right now?") until each enters a real balance — nothing was entered/invented during deployment. Guest is `complete` (demo balance 45000). The full new-user onboarding was verified on the DEV backend only (no safe production test profile). Prior baseline: 93 tx at cutover. Step 4 smoke: production Guest (V2 screen, Add/Undo/Reset) OK; Muhammed's real numbers (balance ₹12,130, flexible −₹14,818) render as BEHIND / ₹0 per day / ₹14,818 short via the deployed bundle; Muhammed/Friend transactions, settings, commitments and balance byte-identical before vs after the deploy.
- **Backups:** `backups/prod_cutover_backup_20260920_061311.json` (API snapshot) and a full Drive copy of the pre-cutover spreadsheet+script (`1DsGzKcdoDPGyF5oc47pzNA6KGK40k9F36xR0Mt7xOgg`); earlier snapshots also in `backups/`. A leftover DEV copy (sheet `1XZhTNlbvEyyTuJEeq7zZXxz8Wh-i7FGMRvQUk7rjx6w`, script `11QPVRXTwXd-…`) with DEV codes exists and is safe to delete.
- **Rollback (do both together):** Step 4 only (frontend) → Netlify deploy `6ab00a1dd3d6617cbc465293` (no backend change needed). Steps 1–3 → Apps Script Version **11** (Sep 20 3:36 PM) + Netlify deploy `6aafb05db0540af6e23c1859` (rollback re-exposes the legacy Pace; V2 settings rows stay harmless). Welcome/code-only → v10 + `6aafa42e8aa7ece91ab3cb27`; Money Plan only → v9 + `6aaf2eb28aa7ecabc9b3cc78`; multi-user → Apps Script v8 (`Code.gs.v8.bak`). Old settings/transactions are untouched by every rollback.
- **Deploy procedure:** backend — replace `Code.gs` in the Apps Script project, Deploy → Manage deployments → New version (URL stays); frontend — zip the 4 `frontend/` files, upload on the pace-ledger Deploys page (never the `/drop` page — new URL). Deploy backend and frontend **together** when the API contract changes. Old cached phones must refresh.

---

## 7. Known limitations

- Not OAuth: anyone with an access code has full access to that profile; codes can't be rotated without editing the hash; session tokens sit in `localStorage`; lockout is per profile (an attacker can lock a profile 15 min).
- All guests share one demo dataset (visible to each other; `Reset demo` restores).
- Currency choice is per-device (not synced / not in the Sheet). Timezone = device only (no manual selection); a tab open across local midnight corrects on its next GET.
- Optimistic `remaining_pace`/`status` are a best-effort mirror until reconcile; a failed Add surfaces after up to ~8–30s (timeout+retry) while the UI stays consistent.
- Undo is single-item; Edit is amount+note only (no date/type edits); corrections act on today's entries only.
- Friend's income/savings/fixed are edited by the owner in `SET_FRIEND`. Validly-signed *expired* tokens can't be tested externally (expiry covered by the simulation).
- Old Apps Script CacheService idempotency window is 90s (fine for an immediate retry only).

---

## 8. PARKED (do NOT implement or plan without an explicit new decision)

- **Custom financial period start day / salary cycle** (e.g. 25th→24th): the algorithm assumes calendar months (`days_in_month`, month-prefix filtering); needs an explicit product/algorithm decision.
- **Minimum realistic daily spend** (pace can fall below what a user realistically needs; would warn, never auto-change the savings target). Related concept: committed expenses vs a flexible spending pool.
- **Savings recovery** (optionally recovering a monthly savings shortfall over later months; never auto-raise the target).
- **Emergency fund.**
- **PWA** (manifest, service worker, iOS standalone metadata) — intentionally postponed.
- Also not planned: manual timezone selection, server-side/synced currency, Undo stack, date editing, real authentication/DB/per-user backends (revisit only if the user base outgrows this MVP).

## 9. Roadmap

Current phase = **real-world validation** (~30 days) with owner + friend + guest visitors. Observe actual behavior; let evidence decide what (if anything) comes next. Origin evidence: a fixed daily allowance failed under unexpected expenses → dynamic model; real use shows the Pace number creates useful awareness (treat as observation, not proven outcome).

## 10. Development rules

1. Read this file first; inspect the code before changing it.
2. Do NOT change the Pace algorithm, the backend, or the locked UI without an explicit instruction; no unnecessary architecture; preserve working behavior; don't ship features just because they're possible.
3. **Never run `setupSheet()` in Apps Script — it wipes Settings.** Select the intended function (e.g. `migrateToMultiUser`, which is copy-only/idempotent) explicitly.
4. Backend/data changes: fresh backup first (API snapshot + Drive copy), test on a DEV copy, verify counts/hashes against the backup, keep legacy data, never write secrets (codes/hashes/tokens) into source or docs.
5. Tests: `node tests/backend_sim.js` (real `Code.gs` in an Apps Script simulation, 111 checks incl. cross-user isolation + Money Plan) · `tests/dev_server.js` (real backend over local HTTP for browser E2E) · `tests/dev_runtime.js` (real DEV web app, 35 checks; refuses the production URL). Use mocked/intercepted POSTs or DEV data — do not write test rows to production (remove any that are created).
6. Ops quirks: automation-driven Chrome is often "hidden" (screenshots/dropdowns fail; drive via DOM/JS, keyboard events open Material menus; Apps Script pages never reach `document_idle`); Netlify uploads work via the file input; the browser pane caches CSS/JS (cache-bust when testing).
7. Update this file when a decision changes; keep it compact.

## 11. Major-decision changelog

- **Concept:** dynamic trajectory replaced fixed daily allowance after real use showed its limits.
- **Ledger UI** chosen over dial/speedometer after review; direction now locked (§4).
- **Performance:** instant cache startup → optimistic Add → timeout/one-retry (idempotent via `client_id`).
- **Safety:** large-expense confirmation; stable `transaction_id`, Undo/Edit/Delete (backend reopened only for identity/corrections), later made optimistic with surgical rollback.
- **Multi-currency V1** (display-only) and **device-local day** (client sends `today`; backend v8).
- **Multi-user:** Google OAuth abandoned → access codes + signed sessions + per-profile tabs + Guest; DEV-verified (sim 64/64, real runtime 35/35), then **production cutover 2026-09-20 (Version 9)**, smoke-tested, count 93 preserved.
- **Money Plan V1 deployed 2026-09-20 (Apps Script v10):** in-app setup/edit of income, savings, commitments; period-start day deliberately left out (calendar-month algorithm). Sim 111/111; dev_runtime 35/35 (DEV still on v9 code — the classifier blocked pushing v10 to DEV, so `saveMoneyPlan` is covered by the sim + prod smoke test).
- **Parked:** minimum daily spend / committed expenses, savings recovery, emergency fund, PWA (§8).
